{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require schools to exclude absence for chicken pox & measles in pupil attendance",
        "additional_details": "A child with 100% attendance can see this drop by 10% due to being required to be absent from school with measles or chickenpox. We believe this is unfair and can be upsetting for children who want to achieve 100% attendance. This feels like punishment especially when schools have rewards for good attendance.",
        "background": "School policies prevent children from attending school if they have chicken pox or measles to help prevent an outbreak. Schools should be banned from counting these absences towards an individual child's attendance percentage which could stop them receiving a good attendance record. ",
